Marine Terminal segment consists of coal export terminal operations in the Port of Baltimore. The company was formerly known as CONSOL Energy Inc. and changed its name to Core Natural Resources, Inc. in January 2025. Core Natural Resources, Inc. was founded in 1864 and is headquartered in Canonsburg, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. James A. Brock | Executive Chairman & CEO | Age 68 | Compensation: $3.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 4K people. Revenue per employee of $859K ranks in the below the sector median among Energy peers, improving at 14%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $4K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Core Natural Resources, Inc. is a mid-cap energy business with a $3.9B market cap on $4.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +26% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 23% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 14-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $21M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 1 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin -4.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 6.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 2.5% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_